course: dictionary
lesson: 2670
title: Diagnose: find out what is wrong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To diagnose something means to find out what is wrong with it. A doctor diagnoses an illness by examining you and studying your symptoms, which are the signs your body shows, like a cough or a fever. A mechanic diagnoses a fault in a car by checking the engine and the wires.
explain: «As a child, Lionel Messi was diagnosed with a growth hormone problem.» The words «diagnosed with» tell you that a doctor checked him and found the problem. Test your meaning: «was found to have a growth hormone problem» still makes sense, so diagnose means find out what the illness is.
explain: Diagnose is a verb, so it changes: diagnose, diagnoses, diagnosed, diagnosing. You can also say diagnose a problem or diagnose the fault. A joke label like «midlife crisis» is not a fact about someone's mind, so it is unkind to use it as if you could diagnose a person that way.
fact: To diagnose means to find out what illness someone has, or what the cause of a problem is.
fact: Doctors diagnose illnesses, and mechanics diagnose faults in cars and machines.
fact: «Diagnosed with» tells the reader that someone has been checked and found to have an illness.
fact: «Stars had setbacks too: as a child Lionel Messi was diagnosed with a growth hormone problem.» A setback is a problem that slows you down.
fact: Diagnose has four forms: diagnose, diagnoses, diagnosed and diagnosing.
exercise: «As a child, Lionel Messi was diagnosed with a growth hormone problem.» What does diagnosed mean here? | Given a prize for growing | Moved to a new house | Sent home from school for a rest | *Found to have, after a check
exercise: A mechanic listens to an engine that will not start and checks the wires. What is the mechanic trying to do? | Wash the car | Paint the car | *Diagnose the fault | Sell the car
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that is a form of diagnose: «Stars had setbacks too, and as a child Lionel Messi was diagnosed with a growth hormone problem.» | setbacks | *diagnosed | growth | Messi
test: Why does the author say diagnosing a person with a joke label is unkind? | It is a joke, and jokes are always kind | It makes the person taller | It means you are a doctor | *It treats someone as if they have a problem, without proof
test: Which phrase means the same as «diagnose a problem»? | Ignore the problem | Hide the problem | Make the problem bigger | *Find the cause of the problem
exam: Yesterday, Dr Lee ___ the cough as a cold. Which word fits the gap? | diagnose | *diagnosed | diagnoses | diagnosing
